This directory vendors `tanimoto_similarity.py` and `butina_cluster.py`
(with a small, marked modification: an added `progress` parameter gating
the tqdm bars) from:

    https://github.com/rowansci/chalcedon
    commit 92da3cc5bd6ffb0d397cb49ea556f168d1d38b7e

chalcedon requires Python >=3.14 as installed from PyPI, but its source
uses no 3.14-only syntax; vendoring lets cosmolayer (Python >=3.10) use
its faster Butina implementation without raising its own Python floor.

